    "previous_model_response": "The marked angle is \\(\\angle BAC=30^\\circ\\).\n\n1. \\(\\angle BAC\\) is an inscribed angle intercepting arc \\(BC\\), so  \n   \\[\n   m\\widehat{BC}=2(30^\\circ)=60^\\circ.\n   \\]\n\n2. Since \\(AB\\) is a diameter, the upper semicircle measures \\(180^\\circ\\). Thus  \n   \\[\n   m\\widehat{AC}=180^\\circ-60^\\circ=120^\\circ.\n   \\]\n\n3. Given \\(\\widehat{AD}=\\widehat{CD}\\), each is half of \\(\\widehat{AC}\\):  \n   \\[\n   m\\widehat{CD}=60^\\circ.\n   \\]\n\n4. \\(\\angle DAC\\) is an inscribed angle intercepting arc \\(DC\\), so  \n   \\[\n   \\angle DAC=\\frac{1}{2}(60^\\circ)=30^\\circ.\n   \\]\n\nCorrect option: C. 30°",
